Would be very nice yes.

I believe this could fit in an option of the hierarchicalMenu widget, something like:

``` js
hierarchicalMenu({
  // ... other parameters
  breadcrumb: {
    container: ...,
    [template: .... (have a default template)]
  }
});
```

having a POC would be great. We then need to define what's the data sent to the template, an array would be the easiest and straightforward.

As for now this can be done like this:

``` js
var breadCrumb: {
  render: function(params) {
    console.log(params.helper.getHierarchicalFacetBreadcrumb('nameOfHierarchicalFacet');
  }
};
```

Then use it anywhere

What am I doing wrong in the code below?  Then render function is never called.

```js
search.addWidget(
  instantsearch.widgets.hierarchicalMenu({
	container: '#Classifications',
	attributes: ['Classifications.lvl0', 'Classifications.lvl1', 'Classifications.lvl2', 'Classifications.lvl3'],
	templates: {
	  header: '<div style="font-size: medium;">Classifications</div>',
	  item: '<a href="javascript:void(0);" originalAttribute="href" originalPath="javascript:void(0);" class="facet-item {{#isRefined}}active{{/isRefined}}"><span class="facet-name"><em class="fa fa-angle-right"></em> {{name}}</span class="facet-name"><span>&nbsp;({{count}})</span></a>'
	},
	breadcrumb: {
	  render: function(params) {
            console.log(params.helper.getHierarchicalFacetBreadcrumb('Classifications'));
            return;
	  }
	}
  })
);
```

@slimtimbodin Back then we decided not to implement a breadcrumb option / widget.

However you can make a custom widget:

```js
var search = instantsearch();
search.addWidget({
    render: function(params) {
      console.log(params.helper.getHierarchicalFacetBreadcrumb('Classifications'));
      // do the actual rendering here using jQuery or any library
    }
});
```
